# Instructions

Assess ONLY state.checks.{{ name }}, identified by source_order in local_raw_evidence.target_page.layouts. Other sources or questions cannot decide this one.

Does the WHOLE source have a positive, identifiable place in the main reading sequence, rather than being page apparatus? Use the original printed arrangement and neighboring reading text. bbox_normalized is [left,top,right,bottom] in page fractions from 0 to 1; near top=0 or bottom=1 is the physical page edge, not the start or end of the story.

Require an actual reading-content role, such as a section/volume opening in the reading columns or an instructional step among the main instructions. Its mentioning a book name, chapter, printing or pages does not turn it into page apparatus. Judge placement and role of the entire source, not just familiar content words.

A marginal folio, running header/footer or publication continuation cue is not main reading, even if it names a chapter. On a blank page, a bottom-margin chapter label does not become a chapter opening just because it is the first or only source. Conversely a genuine section-title leaf can have only its centrally placed title. Do not infer a reading role from the source having been retained by OCR.

Do not judge spelling, paragraph joins or note-reference completeness. Uncertainty about an apparatus role alone is not positive proof of main reading. Require concrete main-reading placement/function; otherwise answer false.

# True

The complete source has a demonstrated main-reading role in this local printed sequence.

# False

Such a complete-source main-reading role is not established; it may be apparatus or uncertain.
